## Do the errors follow 1/sqrt(n)?

Yes, as far as four single estimates can show (`figures/error_vs_n.png`).

- Every error is within its expected single-run spread (error/sigma between 0.13 and 1.26; sum of squares 2.70 on 4 dof, p = 0.61).
- The log-log OLS slope over the four points is -0.65 (SE 0.21). Under an exact n^-1/2 law, a 4-point slope from single estimates falls in [-0.94, -0.06] in 95% of simulations, so -0.65 is consistent with -0.5. The non-monotone step from 1e7 to 1e8 is ordinary fluctuation (error/sigma 0.13 and 0.70).
- Four single draws cannot pin the exponent down (the t-interval is [-1.54, +0.24]). A robustness check, computed off the cluster with independent replicates for n = 1e2 to 1e8, gives an RMS error of 1.659 n^(-0.5017 +- 0.0019) against theory 1.642 n^(-1/2) (`results/ensemble.csv`). This check is not part of the cluster sweep.

## Long run

`long.sbatch` (3e7 samples), first submission, job 53951217: started 12:47:26 and was cancelled by SIGTERM at 12:48:23 (57 s in, during its padding sleep) and did not complete. Our position issued no cancel command; the cause is outside our commands. Its sampling had finished (estimate 3.14108947). It was resubmitted once, unchanged, as job 53951746, which COMPLETED at 13:21:17 (elapsed 30:05, exit 0, `long done`). Estimate 3.14108947, absolute error 5.032e-4, error/sigma = 1.68 (sigma = 3.0e-4), within the expected spread and consistent with the rate (both runs share the same seed, so the estimate is identical).

